Description:
The following query returns one row, while it should given an error saying "Subquery returns more than one row":

CREATE TABLE t0 (c0 INTEGER);
INSERT INTO t0 VALUES (1);
SELECT (SELECT t0.c0 GROUP BY t0.c0 WITH ROLLUP) FROM t0;

What happens here is that the inner query satisfied a set of conditions so that the column is pulled out to the outer query (happens in Item_singlerow_subselect::select_transformer). Without the ROLLUP, this simplification would have been valid. With ROLLUP, this simplification is not valid anymore as the inner query now can return more than one row.

How to repeat:
CREATE TABLE t0 (c0 INTEGER);
INSERT INTO t0 VALUES (1);
SELECT (SELECT t0.c0 GROUP BY t0.c0 WITH ROLLUP) FROM t0;

The above line should return an error, and not one row as it currently does.

Suggested fix:
